{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A transient merge failure followed by an approval dismissal during retry backoff lets the retry bypass the current-approval check."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A PR with more than twenty reviewers can have an outstanding change request omitted from the evidence used by the new approval gate."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A later neutral review can hide an unresolved change request and allow the approval gate to pass."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An in-flight observation or backward clock adjustment can spuriously requeue an entry, but a fresh direct check parks it again."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A partial GraphQL response can spuriously release a waiting entry, but the subsequent direct check rejects the incomplete evidence."}]}